  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Every public method that takes a CancellationToken takes it last and optional (= default), so a caller that does not cancel leaves it out. EnsureTablesAsync is a method of every entity database (EntityDatabase<TDb>), whatever the project references: it creates the model's missing tables and returns them, to seed. Once a database has a migration, its generated class hides EnsureTablesAsync with an error-level [Obsolete] that names MigrateAsync, and a database with a migration history refuses it at run time too. Code compiled against 0.3.0 must be recompiled.",
